# Private working notes — mine, not the submission's.
#
# HANDOVER.md is a handbook written for my own use: how everything works, every
# address, the mistakes and what they taught. It duplicates what the README,
# docs/architecture.md and docs/decisions.md already say for a reader, in a form
# meant for me and for whatever tool I hand this to next. It stays out of the
# repository so that what is published is the project, not my notes about it.
/HANDOVER.md
/private/

# Not part of the submission.
# ETHGlobal asks for the code the demo shows and a history that proves when it
# was written. It does not ask for the shooting script, the brand guide or the
# renders made for the submission form, and those are the product around the
# prototype rather than the prototype. They stay on my machine.
/docs/video-script.md
/web/brand/README.md
/web/brand/ethglobal/
